# Sky whale body plan — BULL variant. A candidate body plan, not the
# live whale: ships/whale.ship is still the one the game and the tests
# load. Preview this one without booting the game:
#
#   godot --headless --path . --script tools/ship_preview.gd -- ships/whale_bull.ship
#
# The bull is the alpha ram of the sky: a 30-wide profile against the
# reference whale's 26, and it carries its extra tonnage lengthwise, not
# upward — the 4-row thickness cap of the owner's survey (2026-08-20) is
# never exceeded. Bulk comes from head mass instead. Where the reference
# tapers to a rounded snout, the bull's head runs the FULL 4 rows all the
# way to the right edge and stops square, with a 3-cell gape cut under it
# for the heavy underslung jaw. The tail is the survey's thin part (2
# rows through the peduncle), opening into a broad forked fluke: the two
# left-hand tips with the notch bitten out between them.
#
# The three empty cells in row 1 are the STOMACH cavity (swallowed loot
# lives there once items exist; the compartment is real today — mine in
# and you break through into a hollow). Note the gape at the bottom
# right is NOT the stomach: it is open to the sky, a mouth, not a room.
#
#   W  blubber (buoyant flesh — keep it the majority or the whale falls)
#   M  meat (dense core, shelled in blubber on every outside face)
#
# 101 cells, 78 blubber (77%). It floats because it is mostly blubber —
# mining the blubber off a carcass literally sinks it. One connected
# piece; the fluke tips hang off the peduncle, not off each other.

# HEADERS (2026-09-05) — what this file already was, said out loud, so the
# drafting table can file it. Header lines only: the grid below is untouched.
name Bull Whale
kind whale

origin 15 1

WWW.....WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW
.WWWWWWWWWMMMMM...MMMMMWWWWWWW
.WWWWWWWWWMMMMMMMMMMMMMWWWWWWW
WWW......WWWWWWWWWWWWWW...WWWW
